    "blocks": [
      {
        "id": "p1",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "Cormorant",
            "zh": "鸬鹚"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " fishing is a traditional skill in Asia. It is useful for catching fish from narrow rivers. The skill was invented in China more than 1,300 years ago. It then spread to Japan, Korea, and India."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p2",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "In the 17th century, cormorant fishing was introduced into European "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "courts",
            "zh": "宫廷"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". King Louis XIII of France built many ponds for his cormorants. He enjoyed watching the birds display their skills to him. In England, King James I also trained many cormorants and built ponds for them. Soon, cormorant fishing became popular all over Europe. French fishermen even dressed like Chinese fishermen when they were practising cormorant fishing!"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p3",
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": "Today, cormorant fishing can still be seen in China and Japan. Chinese fishermen usually work in daylight. In Japan, fishermen usually work at night under the light of torches. It takes a lot of training to make cormorants catch fish for men. The best cormorants are those raised by the fisherman himself. The fisherman carefully "
          },
          {
            "t": "gloss",
            "v": "tends",
            "zh": "照料"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": " his young birds. He talks to them every two to three hours. Fishermen must pay attention to their cormorants’ personalities. They must make sure the birds don’t fight among themselves. When it is done correctly, cormorants are "
          },
          {
            "t": "underline",
            "v": "fishing machines"
          },
          {
            "t": "text",
            "v": ". Some birds can catch more than 150 fish in an hour!"
          }
        ]
      }
    ]
  },
